#!/bin/bash
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." || exit 1
R="Research canon+fan attacks (WebSearch/WebFetch)."
tools/run_agent.sh fen Fen "REBUILD Fen bigger and far scarier (user request). Refs: docs/ref/confirmed/fen_new.jpg (very tall, thin; huge orange-red hair like a flowing mane/tail with an ahoge, black short-sleeve tee, rolled blue denim shorts, bandaged legs, bare feet with black claws, arms ending in LONG black blade-like claws hanging almost to the ground), docs/ref/confirmed/fen.jpg and docs/ref/confirmed/fen_vs_alice.jpg (right side: Fen's black monster silhouette with red eyes and spindly clawed limbs). SIZE: canon 305 cm is the tallest of the cast but the user wants Fen to look clearly BIGGER than Miss Circle (2.92 blocks): make the model about 3.6 blocks tall (max cube top y ~58) and set the hitbox in ModEntities to about 1.0 x 3.2 (+ shadow in FenSpec). POWER: Fen is very strong in canon: raise attributes in Fen.attributes() (e.g. ~260 health, damage ~11, some armor/knockback resistance) and give 14-16 abilities. SHAPE-SHIFTING ARMS: Fen can reshape the arms at will into monstrous weapons - make these real attacks with their own model parts + animations: giant scythe/blade arms, whip/tentacle arms with long reach, spear/needle volleys, shield/wing arms for guarding and gliding, hammer/mace arm slams, many extra spidery arms, grab-and-pull hooks, a maw/jaw arm that bites. Also a MONSTER MODE: at <50% hp (or via setStance(1)) she becomes the black red-eyed monster of fen_vs_alice.jpg: limbs elongate, hair spikes up, more savage attacks (framework: FpeEntity.getStance()/setStance(int), quad_*/idle swap, see HANDOFF/Alice quad work; use stance 1 for monster mode animations 'quad_idle'/'quad_walk' or ability gating with .when(e -> e.getStance()==1)). Keep her melee-focused (meleeFocus() is already true): gap closers, no sit-and-shoot. Fully authored animations for every attack. $R"
tools/run_agent.sh fen Fen "SIZE PASS FOR THE WHOLE CAST (user request: make every character about as big as in canon / fan works). Do NOT rebuild models: write tools/bbgen/rescale.py (uniformly scale a .bbmodel: cube from/to/origin/inflate, group origins, 'position' keyframes; see how fen.bbmodel was scaled earlier in git history if useful) and apply it. Research canon heights (WebSearch/WebFetch: FPE wiki, height charts, 'FPE size comparison'; known data point: chart lists Fen 305 cm, Miss Circle 292 cm, Miss Grace 273 cm, Miss Sasha 216 cm, Kevin 180 cm, Abbie 157 cm; 1 block = 100 cm). Characters: miss_circle, miss_thavel, miss_bloomie, red_circle, danger_thavel, danger_bloomie, alice (+boss), danger_alice (+boss), green_* , mutant_* , infected_bloomie, infected_zip, aiden, riley, daniel_barrel, hansel_juvenile, lord_hansel. Where no source exists, estimate from the confirmed art relative to the known heights and say so. Rules: Fen stays the tallest humanoid and must be >= 3.6 blocks (another agent just rebuilt her - do not rescale Fen); Miss Circle = 2.92 blocks (already). Write docs/HEIGHTS.md (table: character, canon cm + source or 'estimate', old height, new height). Apply: rescale each bbmodel (height measured as max cube top y /16 in the rest pose; keep boss/phase-2 giants proportional), update hitboxes in registry/ModEntities.java (width ~ 0.25*height, height ~ 0.88*model height) and the shadow radius in the *Spec.java load calls, and fix any hard-coded EntityDimensions in the character classes (getDimensions) proportionally. Make sure the server ability reach values do not become silly (do not edit abilities). You may edit those framework registry/spec files for this task. Final report: the table."
echo QUEUE_DONE
